  <ADXVALUE id="RAW_00" idhash="0xEF4401A6" title="Static 1 / echo">
    <desc>Was 1 in all logs and never changed, I assumed it was some static value/flag.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;According to claude its &quot;local-ID echo (=01)&quot;, ram address (none)&#013;&#010;confidence high</desc>
    <flags>0x0000000C</flags>
    <parentcmdidhash>0xDAA83ACD</parentcmdidhash>
    <units>Static 1 / echo</units>
    <packetoffset>0x00</packetoffset>
    <range low="0.000000" high="2.000000" />
    <alarms low="0.000000" high="2.000000" />
    <digcount>1</digcount>
    <outputtype>1</outputtype>
    <MATH equation="X">
      <VAR varID="X" type="native" />
    </MATH>
  </ADXVALUE>

  <ADXVALUE id="BATTREYVOLTAGE" idhash="0xD5E2F749" title="battery voltage">
    <desc>Same as KSW_dmg210 adx. Tracked voltage, tested using variable power supply, equation may be slightly off.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;according to claude the ram address is 0xE04F</desc>
    <parentcmdidhash>0xDAA83ACD</parentcmdidhash>
    <units>battery voltage (V)</units>
    <packetoffset>0x01</packetoffset>
    <range low="0.000000" high="20.000000" />
    <alarms low="0.000000" high="255.000000" />
    <digcount>1</digcount>
    <outputtype>3</outputtype>
    <datatype>66</datatype>
    <unittype>32</unittype>
    <MATH equation="0.1015625 * X">
      <VAR varID="X" type="native" />
    </MATH>
  </ADXVALUE>

  <ADXVALUE id="RAW_02" idhash="0xEF441546" title="Battery Status Flags *">
    <desc>during logs it was normally 13, while it was 5 when cranking. was unable to confirm what it was on my own.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;According to claude its battery status flags&#013;&#010;Bit 1 = supply voltage valid&#013;&#010;Bit 2 = voltage above C_VB_MIN_JUMP&#013;&#010;Bit 3 = both channels &gt;=C_VB_MIN_OBD1&#013;&#010;Bit 4 = both &gt;=C_VB_MIN_OBD2&#013;&#010;Bit 5 = &quot;BFD16.12, a copy of digital input BFD76.14, A digital input pin, sampled every main-loop pass (0x5FD24). I couldn&#226;&#128;&#153;t identify the pin.&quot;&#013;&#010;Bit 6 &quot;BFD16.11, Set in the main loop when init is done and the pin above is set. It then skips many tasks, so it behaves like an after-run/shutdown flag.&quot;&#013;&#010;ram address 0xC245&#013;&#010;confidence &quot;high&quot; for bits 1-4&#013;&#010;&quot;Low&quot; for bit 5&#013;&#010;&quot;Low-medium&quot; for bit 6&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;I havent independently tested/confirmed, bits 5 and 6 wernt ever high in my logs</desc>
    <parentcmdidhash>0xDAA83ACD</parentcmdidhash>
    <units>Battery Status Flags ?</units>
    <packetoffset>0x02</packetoffset>
    <range low="0.000000" high="63.000000" />
    <alarms low="0.000000" high="255.000000" />
    <digcount>1</digcount>
    <outputtype>1</outputtype>
    <datatype>2</datatype>
    <MATH equation="X">
      <VAR varID="X" type="native" />
    </MATH>
  </ADXVALUE>

  <ADXVALUE id="COOLTANTVOLTAG" idhash="0xCDA1CF63" title="Coolant temp sensor voltage">
    <desc>moved with coollant temperature, responded to unplugging coolant temp sensor.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;according to Claude the ram address is 0xE1B3</desc>
    <parentcmdidhash>0xDAA83ACD</parentcmdidhash>
    <units>Coolant temp sensor voltage (V)</units>
    <packetoffset>0x03</packetoffset>
    <range low="0.000000" high="5.000000" />
    <alarms low="0.000000" high="255.000000" />
    <digcount>2</digcount>
    <outputtype>3</outputtype>
    <datatype>1</datatype>
    <unittype>32</unittype>
    <MATH equation="X * 5 / 255">
      <VAR varID="X" type="native" />
    </MATH>
  </ADXVALUE>

  <ADXVALUE id="COOLANTTEMPERA" idhash="0x4F4046E6" title="Coolant Temperature">
    <desc>Followed cooant temperature, increased when I heated area around coolant temp sensor. Same byte as KSW_dmg210 adx but different equation.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;according to Claude the ram address is 0xC5B1</desc>
    <parentcmdidhash>0xDAA83ACD</parentcmdidhash>
    <units>Coolant temp (C)</units>
    <packetoffset>0x04</packetoffset>
    <range low="-48.000000" high="143.000000" />
    <alarms low="0.000000" high="255.000000" />
    <digcount>1</digcount>
    <outputtype>3</outputtype>
    <datatype>13</datatype>
    <unittype>15</unittype>
    <MATH equation="(X - 64) * 0.75">
      <VAR varID="X" type="native" />
    </MATH>
  </ADXVALUE>

  <ADXVALUE id="INTAKETEMPVOLT" idhash="0x81380223" title="Intake air temp sensor voltage">
    <desc>Responded to disconnecting intake temp sensor, going to 255 (5v) when I did, moved with intake temp.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;according to Claude the ram address is 0xC5B9</desc>
