  <ADXVALUE id="RAW_18" idhash="0xEF45C386" title="0X18 Static 0 ?">
    <desc>Was 0 in all logs and never changed.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;According to claude its &quot;Status/validity byte loaded with those same adaptation values (copied to C3B1, and cleared to 0 together with the CE24/CE1C words when the key doesn&#226;&#128;&#153;t match).&quot; those adapatation values its referring to are 0X52/0X53 and 0X54/0X55 which were also static 0 values in my testing&#013;&#010;its 0 because &quot;Adaptation not valid&quot;&#013;&#010;ram address 0xC3B0&#013;&#010;It gave a medium-low confidence for this value</desc>
    <flags>0x00000004</flags>
    <parentcmdidhash>0xDAA83ACD</parentcmdidhash>
    <units>0X18 Static 0 ?</units>
    <packetoffset>0x18</packetoffset>
    <range low="0.000000" high="1.000000" />
    <alarms low="0.000000" high="1.000000" />
    <digcount>1</digcount>
    <outputtype>1</outputtype>
    <datatype>2</datatype>
    <unittype>2</unittype>
    <MATH equation="X">
      <VAR varID="X" type="native" />
    </MATH>
  </ADXVALUE>

  <ADXVALUE id="RAW_19?" idhash="0xE8BA85BD" title="0X19 (pair with 0x1A) Cam sensor edge position*">
    <desc>Couldnt figure out exact meaning, seemed to be effected by tests with cam position sensor though.&#013;&#010;paired with 0x1A. Normally 0x19=39 and 0x1A=99, 0/0 when cam sensor was disconnected before key on, frozen if cam sensor lost with engine off, once swapped from 39/99 to 99/39  after reconnecting cam sensor after start, flickered 39/40 with injector 2 disconnected.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;according to claude &quot;Verified in the firmware: Both 0x19 and 0x1A are copies of the same capture register (FC0F), stored in C28A when BFD2C.3 = 0 and in C28B when BFD2C.3 = 1, i.e. one value per cam-signal edge. Values are crank positions in 6 degree steps over a 120 step (720 deg) cycle. The cam diagnosis (0x5A5xx) checks them against 38 and 98 with a tolerance of C_CAM_DYW_DIAG (8), which matches the normal 39 / 99.&#013;&#010;Which edge is which: not proven.&quot;&#013;&#010;ram address 0xC28A&#013;&#010;Confidence: high for the meaning.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;I cant safely which edge is which so its staying u</desc>
    <parentcmdidhash>0xDAA83ACD</parentcmdidhash>
    <units>Cam sensor edge position</units>
    <packetoffset>0x19</packetoffset>
    <range low="0.000000" high="120.000000" />
    <alarms low="0.000000" high="255.000000" />
    <digcount>1</digcount>
    <outputtype>1</outputtype>
    <datatype>2</datatype>
    <unittype>2</unittype>
    <MATH equation="X">
      <VAR varID="X" type="native" />
    </MATH>
  </ADXVALUE>

  <ADXVALUE id="RAW_1A" idhash="0xEF45D7C6" title="0X1A (pair with 0x19) Cam sensor edge position*">
    <desc>see 0X19 description for meaning&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;See 0x19. RAM 0xC28B (the BFD2C.3 = 1 capture).</desc>
    <parentcmdidhash>0xDAA83ACD</parentcmdidhash>
    <units>Cam sensor edge position</units>
    <packetoffset>0x1A</packetoffset>
    <range low="0.000000" high="120.000000" />
    <alarms low="0.000000" high="255.000000" />
    <digcount>1</digcount>
    <outputtype>1</outputtype>
    <datatype>2</datatype>
    <unittype>2</unittype>
    <MATH equation="X">
      <VAR varID="X" type="native" />
    </MATH>
  </ADXVALUE>

  <ADXVALUE id="RAW_1B" idhash="0xEF45CDA6" title="0X1B TCU1 transmission CAN message Flag?">
    <desc>Was 0 in all logs and never changed.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;According to claude its &quot;Flag byte: bit 0 = (E045 &amp; 7) &#226;&#137;&#160; 0, bit 1 = bit 3 of E045. E045 sits in the code that handles the TCU1 transmission CAN message (C_ABC_*_TIMEOUT_TCU1_DIAG).&quot;&#013;&#010;ram address 0xC246&#013;&#010;it gave a medium confidence rating&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;I have a 6 spd so I cant test this&#013;&#010;</desc>
    <flags>0x00000004</flags>
    <parentcmdidhash>0xDAA83ACD</parentcmdidhash>
    <units>0X1B TCU1 transmission CAN message Flag?</units>
    <packetoffset>0x1B</packetoffset>
    <range low="0.000000" high="3.000000" />
    <alarms low="0.000000" high="1.000000" />
    <digcount>1</digcount>
    <outputtype>1</outputtype>
    <datatype>2</datatype>
    <unittype>2</unittype>
    <MATH equation="X">
      <VAR varID="X" type="native" />
    </MATH>
  </ADXVALUE>

  <ADXVALUE id="ACFLAG" idhash="0x5E19DB69" title="AC flag*">
    <desc>Was 0 with ac off, 1 with ac on, was only 0/1 in logs. If there are any other flags in this byte im unaware of them&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;according to claude &quot;Verified in the firmware: built at 0x74BD6 from four bits: value 1 = BFD72.4 (the A/C flag), 2 = BFD72.5, 4 = BFD78.9, 8 = BFD72.1. Only the value-1 bit was ever seen. Equation X is correct (1 = A/C on); if one of the other bits is ever set the reading will be above 1, so treat AC = (X mod 2).&quot;&#013;&#010;ram address 0xC247&#013;&#010;Confidence: high.</desc>
    <flags>0x00000004</flags>
    <parentcmdidhash>0xDAA83ACD</parentcmdidhash>
    <units>AC flag*</units>
    <packetoffset>0x1C</packetoffset>
    <range low="-0.100000" high="1.100000" />
    <alarms low="0.000000" high="2.000000" />
    <digcount>1</digcount>
    <outputtype>1</outputtype>
    <datatype>3</datatype>
    <MATH equation="X">
      <VAR varID="X" type="native" />
    </MATH>
  </ADXVALUE>

  <ADXVALUE id="O2VOLTSB1UP" idhash="0xEEBC5D65" title="Upstream O2 voltage bank 1">
    <desc>flickered between high and low values, whether it was high or low correlated with if stft bank 1 was increaseing/decreasing&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;according to Claude the ram address is 0xE242</desc>
    <parentcmdidhash>0xDAA83ACD</parentcmdidhash>
    <units>Upstream O2 voltage bank 1 (V)</units>
    <packetoffset>0x1D</packetoffset>
    <range low="0.000000" high="5.000000" />
    <alarms low="0.000000" high="255.000000" />
    <digcount>2</digcount>
    <outputtype>3</outputtype>
    <datatype>58</datatype>
    <unittype>32</unittype>
    <MATH equation="0.0195887 * X">
      <VAR varID="X" type="native" />
    </MATH>
  </ADXVALUE>

  <ADXVALUE id="O2VOLTSB2UP" idhash="0xEED6DD65" title="Upstream O2 voltage bank 2">
    <desc>behaved the same way as Upstream O2 voltage bank 1, but for bank 2 stft.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;according to Claude the ram address is 0xE336</desc>
