  <ADXVALUE id="RAW_37" idhash="0xEF457AC6" title="Start of injection angle *">
    <desc>Rpm dependent: 88 crank, ~50 idle, ~35 at 1400 rpm, 19-73 part load.&#013;&#010;0 when engine runs without cam position, starts normal 2-3 s then 0, recovers at next start or on cam sensor reconnection.&#013;&#010;couldnt figure it out from logs alone&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;according to calude &quot;Verified in the firmware: SOI (start of injection) raw value, built at 0x6AA40-0x6ABD8 from IP_SOI__N_32__TI_MV (running) or IP_SOI_ST__N_32__TI_MV (start; first value 88 = your cranking value) plus two signed corrections, then clamped to 0..100. With the cam-fault flag set it uses C_SOI_CAM_DIAG (= 0), which is the &apos;0 without cam sync&apos; behaviour. Both tables use -6*X+180 degrees, so the equation is confirmed and the range is -420..180.&quot;&#013;&#010; ram address 0xFC35&#013;&#010;Confidence: high.</desc>
    <parentcmdidhash>0xDAA83ACD</parentcmdidhash>
    <units>Start of injection angle (deg)</units>
    <packetoffset>0x37</packetoffset>
    <range low="-420.000000" high="180.000000" />
    <alarms low="0.000000" high="255.000000" />
    <digcount>1</digcount>
    <outputtype>1</outputtype>
    <datatype>1</datatype>
    <unittype>23</unittype>
    <MATH equation="180 - 6 * X">
      <VAR varID="X" type="native" />
    </MATH>
  </ADXVALUE>

  <ADXVALUE id="POWERCUT" idhash="0x0EA3066D" title="fuel/power cut level ">
    <desc>When hitting rev limiter or when torque intervention is requested this increases up to a value of 13 (max seen from tcs was 9), Im assuming its fuel/power cut level (13 = full cut), since there are 14 values (0-13) im assuming it correlates to ID_TQR_REL_SCC__PAT_INH_IV&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;according to calude it is &quot;inj inhibit pattern&quot;&#013;&#010;ram address 0xC7B4&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;didnt give confidence level but it seems to match observed behaviour</desc>
    <parentcmdidhash>0xDAA83ACD</parentcmdidhash>
    <units>fuel/power cut level</units>
    <packetoffset>0x38</packetoffset>
    <range low="0.000000" high="15.000000" />
    <alarms low="0.000000" high="255.000000" />
    <digcount>1</digcount>
    <outputtype>1</outputtype>
    <datatype>1</datatype>
    <unittype>2</unittype>
    <MATH equation="X">
      <VAR varID="X" type="native" />
    </MATH>
  </ADXVALUE>

  <ADXVALUE id="CLOSEDLOOPFLAG" idhash="0xCA1D63B9" title="Closed-Loop / Lambda Enable Flags">
    <desc>0 when cold or injectors unplugged (with dtc). 3 once engine is warmed up. stft didnt move when this is 0.  presumably one bit per bank,&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;Confirmed by claude:&#013;&#010;according to claude bit 1 is for bank 1 lambda and bit 2 is bank 2, IP_TI_WUP_IS_LSCL_AT LSCL=lambda closed loop&#013;&#010;ram address is 0xC248&#013;&#010;confidence &quot;Medium-high&quot;</desc>
    <parentcmdidhash>0xDAA83ACD</parentcmdidhash>
    <units>Closed-Loop / Lambda Enable Flags</units>
    <packetoffset>0x39</packetoffset>
    <range low="0.000000" high="3.000000" />
    <alarms low="0.000000" high="255.000000" />
    <digcount>1</digcount>
    <outputtype>1</outputtype>
    <datatype>1</datatype>
    <unittype>2</unittype>
    <MATH equation="X">
      <VAR varID="X" type="native" />
    </MATH>
  </ADXVALUE>

  <ADXVALUE id="STFTB1" idhash="0xF60C0FDD" title="Short Term Fuel Trim Bank 1">
    <desc>behaved as Id expect stft to, fact that it closely matches 0X3B reinforces this since there should be one per bank. Same byte as KSW_dmg210 adx but different equation.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;according to claude the ram address is 0xE1FF</desc>
    <parentcmdidhash>0xDAA83ACD</parentcmdidhash>
    <units>Short Term Fuel Trim Bank 1 (%)</units>
    <packetoffset>0x3A</packetoffset>
    <range low="-50.000000" high="50.000000" />
    <alarms low="0.000000" high="255.000000" />
    <digcount>2</digcount>
    <outputtype>3</outputtype>
    <datatype>50</datatype>
    <unittype>67</unittype>
    <MATH equation="(x-128)/2.56">
      <VAR varID="x" type="native" />
    </MATH>
  </ADXVALUE>

