  <ADXVALUE id="LTFTIDLEB1" idhash="0x540689AF" title="Long Term Fuel Trim Idle Load bank 1 ">
    <desc>based on logs it was a slow learned adaptive value, ltft idle load was best match esp due to being ebtween stft and ltft part load. Same byte as KSW_dmg210 adx. but that equation didnt seem to make sense.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;according to claude &quot;Verified in the firmware: additive injection-time adaptation. Value = (W - 32768) * 0.004 ms, where W = 0x3E + 256*0x3F (0x8000 = 0). Limited to +-125 counts (+-0.5 ms) by C_TI_AD_ADD_MIN/MAX (little-endian 0x7F83 / 0x807D; the XDF shows them byte-swapped). Reset to 0x8000 if out of limits. Your 0x3F range (127-128) fits these limits. The ms unit is inferred from C_TI_MIN = 250 = 1 ms; where it is added to the injection time was not traced.&quot;&#013;&#010;ram address 0xE208-0xE209&#013;&#010;Confidence: high for structure and limits, medium for the ms scale.</desc>
    <flags>0x00000002</flags>
    <parentcmdidhash>0xDAA83ACD</parentcmdidhash>
    <units>Long Term Fuel Trim Idle Load bank 1 (ms)</units>
    <packetoffset>0x3E</packetoffset>
    <sizeinbits>16</sizeinbits>
    <range low="-0.500000" high="0.500000" />
    <alarms low="0.000000" high="255.000000" />
    <digcount>2</digcount>
    <outputtype>3</outputtype>
    <datatype>49</datatype>
    <unittype>85</unittype>
    <MATH equation="(x - 32768)*0.004">
      <VAR varID="x" type="native" />
    </MATH>
  </ADXVALUE>

