  <ADXVALUE id="RAW_48" idhash="0xEF453786" title="Upstream O2 heater PWM factor bank 1?">
    <desc>closely matched with 0x49. initally thought it was downstream o2 sensor duty before i realized thats what 0x4a and 0x4b are, but no longer sure what they are.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;according to claude &quot;Verified in the firmware: this is bank 1 (E2CC sits with E2CE = 0x46, the bank 1 upstream heater), and 0x49 is bank 2. Initialised to C_LSHPWM_FAC_INI (163) and limited by C_LSHPWM_FAC_MIN (64) and C_LSHPWM_FAC_MAX (192); logs show 128-192, the top being exactly the max limit. The PWM output is X*256*25000&gt;&gt;16 on a 25000 count period, so heater duty (0x46/0x4A) is X/2.56 %. What moves this factor after init was not found in code (it is probably updated through a pointer).&quot;&#013;&#010; ram address 0xE2CC&#013;&#010;Confidence: medium.</desc>
    <parentcmdidhash>0xDAA83ACD</parentcmdidhash>
    <units>Upstream O2 heater PWM factor bank 1?</units>
    <packetoffset>0x48</packetoffset>
    <range low="64.000000" high="192.000000" />
    <alarms low="0.000000" high="255.000000" />
    <digcount>2</digcount>
    <outputtype>3</outputtype>
    <datatype>3</datatype>
    <unittype>3</unittype>
    <MATH equation="X">
      <VAR varID="X" type="native" />
    </MATH>
  </ADXVALUE>

  <ADXVALUE id="RAW_49" idhash="0xEF4520C6" title="Upstream O2 heater PWM factor bank 2?">
    <desc>see 0x48 for desctiption&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;according to claude the ram address is 0xE3C0 </desc>
    <parentcmdidhash>0xDAA83ACD</parentcmdidhash>
