  <ADXVALUE id="RAW_4C" idhash="0xEF453C46" title="ISAPWM ">
    <desc>32768 engine off and when starting, ramps down at idle (about 9000 warm idle), rises with rpm with some variation with throttle. higher at higher idle targets. probably iacv duty, unknown equation&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010; according to claude &quot;Verified in the firmware: ISA (idle air actuator) PWM duty, ramped by C_ISAPWM_LGRD and diagnosed with C_ISAPWM_MMV_DIAG / C_MIN_PWM_ISA / C_MAX_PWM_ISA. All 16-bit ISAPWM tables in the XDF use 0.0015258789*X (= X/655.36 %, 65535 = 100 %), and the stored limits come out as round percentages (C_ISAPWM_MAX_I_IS = 9830 = 15 %), so this scale is confirmed.&quot;&#013;&#010;ram address 0xF8E8-0xF8E9&#013;&#010;Confidence: high.</desc>
    <flags>0x00000002</flags>
    <parentcmdidhash>0xDAA83ACD</parentcmdidhash>
    <units>ISAPWM * (%)</units>
    <packetoffset>0x4C</packetoffset>
    <sizeinbits>16</sizeinbits>
    <range low="0.000000" high="100.000000" />
    <alarms low="0.000000" high="255.000000" />
    <digcount>2</digcount>
    <outputtype>3</outputtype>
    <datatype>36</datatype>
    <unittype>67</unittype>
    <MATH equation="X * 0.0015258789">
      <VAR varID="X" type="native" />
    </MATH>
  </ADXVALUE>

  <ADXVALUE id="IDLEINTEGRATOR" idhash="0xE860ED53" title="Idle speed controller output (PID sum)*">
    <desc>0 under load, larger at idle entry then decays down as rpm aproaches idle, larger when rpm and idle rpm target are further appart. Seemed like some kind of idle speed integrator, which is reinnforced by the behaviour of learned idle correction. makes senst to be idle speed related if next to isapwm. formula unknown&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;according to claude &quot;Verified in the firmware: written at 0x61E98. It is the sum of the idle controller terms (CE26 integrator + CE22 + CE36, where CE36 is the P term from IP_ISAPWM_P_IS__N_DIF_COR) multiplied by the gain C3B2, using signed saturating adds, and is forced to 0 when the idle controller is inactive (BFD4C.7/.8). It is a signed 16-bit ISA PWM correction in the same 1/655.36 % units as 0x4C, so the equation is signed(X)*0.0015258789 %. The name &apos;integrator&apos; only describes one of its parts.&quot;&#013;&#010;ram address 0xCE28-0xCE29&#013;&#010;Confidence: medium.</desc>
    <flags>0x00000003</flags>
    <parentcmdidhash>0xDAA83ACD</parentcmdidhash>
    <units>Idle speed controller output (PID sum)? (%)</units>
    <packetoffset>0x4E</packetoffset>
    <sizeinbits>16</sizeinbits>
    <range low="-25.000000" high="25.000000" />
    <alarms low="0.000000" high="255.000000" />
    <digcount>1</digcount>
    <outputtype>1</outputtype>
    <datatype>1</datatype>
    <unittype>3</unittype>
    <MATH equation="X * 0.0015258789">
      <VAR varID="X" type="native" />
    </MATH>
  </ADXVALUE>

  <ADXVALUE id="IDLECORRECTION" idhash="0x2880178F" title="Learned idle correction *">
    <desc>reset to 0 with adaptive values, on exiting idle it steps up or down, with larger steps corresponding to larger values in the idle speed intigrator, this is most likely a learned value for idle speed correction. formula unknown&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;according to claude &quot;Verified in the firmware: a learned (adaptive) ISA PWM correction, low-pass filtered with C_AD_CRLC_IS (routine 0x61EEE), saved to and restored from stored memory (restored at 0x61072, cleared to 0 with the adaptation reset). Signed 16-bit in the same 1/655.36 % units as 0x4C, limited by C_ISAPWM_AD_MIN_IS = -6554 (-10.0 %) and C_ISAPWM_AD_MAX_IS = +9830 (+15.0 %) (little-endian words; the XDF shows them byte-swapped). The round percentages confirm the scale.&quot;&#013;&#010;ram address 0xCDD8-0xCDD9&#013;&#010;Confidence: high.</desc>
    <flags>0x00000003</flags>
    <parentcmdidhash>0xDAA83ACD</parentcmdidhash>
    <units>Learned idle correction * (%)</units>
    <packetoffset>0x50</packetoffset>
    <sizeinbits>16</sizeinbits>
    <range low="-10.000000" high="15.000000" />
    <alarms low="0.000000" high="255.000000" />
    <digcount>2</digcount>
    <outputtype>3</outputtype>
    <datatype>1</datatype>
    <unittype>3</unittype>
    <MATH equation="X * 0.0015258789">
      <VAR varID="X" type="native" />
    </MATH>
  </ADXVALUE>

  <ADXVALUE id="RAW_52" idhash="0xEF47C546" title="0X52 Static 0?">
    <desc>Was 0 in all logs and never changed.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;according to claude 0X52-0X53 and 0X54-0X55 are &quot;Words restored from the stored adaptation record at start, zeroed if the record key doesn&#226;&#128;&#153;t match. They feed F8B6/F8BA through C_ISAPWM_ACCIN_AD_FAC, so they are idle-air (ISA PWM) A/C-load adaptation values.&quot;&#013;&#010;and its zero because &quot;Not learned or not stored&quot;&#013;&#010;ram address 0xCE24&#013;&#010;its confidence level for this is medium</desc>
    <flags>0x00000004</flags>
    <parentcmdidhash>0xDAA83ACD</parentcmdidhash>
    <units>0X52 Static 0?</units>
    <packetoffset>0x52</packetoffset>
    <range low="0.000000" high="1.000000" />
    <alarms low="0.000000" high="1.000000" />
    <digcount>1</digcount>
    <outputtype>1</outputtype>
    <datatype>3</datatype>
    <unittype>3</unittype>
    <MATH equation="X">
      <VAR varID="X" type="native" />
    </MATH>
  </ADXVALUE>

