    </MATH>
  </ADXVALUE>

  <ADXVALUE id="RAW_59" idhash="0xEF47CCC6" title="Evap canister purge demand *">
    <desc>was 0 when ehgine was cold or in open loop , ~13 at closed-loop idle, up to 26 under idle with load load, a 254 spike was seen on a throttle tap. unsure what it could be based on logs.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;according to claude &quot;Verified in the firmware: canister purge (CPS) demand, produced by the routine at 0x59504 and used as the input of IP_CPPWM_CPS__CPPWM (the purge valve duty curve, output eq 0.390625*X %). It is zeroed in the purge-reset routine (0x58EB6) and the purge only runs when lambda control is active (C_LAM_TRA_STATE_MIN), which matches your 0 when cold / open loop. The scaling of this byte itself is not proven (if it follows the curve output it would be X*0.390625 %).&quot;&#013;&#010;ram address 0xC27E&#013;&#010;Confidence: medium-high.</desc>
    <parentcmdidhash>0xDAA83ACD</parentcmdidhash>
    <units>Evap canister purge demand?</units>
    <packetoffset>0x59</packetoffset>
    <range low="0.000000" high="255.000000" />
    <alarms low="0.000000" high="255.000000" />
    <digcount>2</digcount>
    <outputtype>3</outputtype>
    <datatype>12</datatype>
    <unittype>67</unittype>
    <MATH equation="X*0.390625">
      <VAR varID="X" type="native" />
    </MATH>
  </ADXVALUE>

  <ADXVALUE id="IDLETRIM" idhash="0x07D358E6" title="evap purge lambda correction?">
    <desc>I had no idea, suspected idle trim but not enough data to verify.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;according to claude &quot;Verified in the firmware: (offset binary, 0x8000 = 0). It is set to 0x8000 together with the purge demand (0x59) in the purge-reset routine at 0x58EB6, is limited to +-0x5000 (+-62.5 %) by the code at 0x59712-0x59860 (the clamp uses C_LAM_MV_DIF_MAX_1_CP), and is scaled by a ratio (E076/E078) into the lambda correction E066 = 0x8000 + result. That makes it the canister purge fuel (vapour) correction, which can only remove fuel, matching your &apos;never above 0, down to -58 % at hot idle&apos;. E064 is probably the bank 2 counterpart.&#013;&#010;Corrected: it is not an idle trim.&quot;&#013;&#010;ram address 0xE062&#013;&#010;Confidence: medium-low (function inferred from where it is set, cleared and used).</desc>
    <flags>0x00000002</flags>
    <parentcmdidhash>0xDAA83ACD</parentcmdidhash>
    <units>Purge lambda correction (%)</units>
    <packetoffset>0x5A</packetoffset>
    <sizeinbits>16</sizeinbits>
    <range low="-62.500000" high="62.500000" />
    <alarms low="0.000000" high="255.000000" />
    <digcount>1</digcount>
    <outputtype>1</outputtype>
    <datatype>3</datatype>
    <unittype>3</unittype>
    <MATH equation="(X - 32768) / 327.68">
      <VAR varID="X" type="native" />
    </MATH>
  </ADXVALUE>

  <ADXVALUE id="RAW_5C" idhash="0xEF47D046" title="Radiator fan stage">
    <desc>only 1/0 in logs which seems like a flag. typically switches for on for ~15-180s, about 100 s on/off in a longer log with pleanty of sitting in traffic where it correlates to coolant temperature changes. Fits behaviour of radiator fan.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010; according to claude &quot;Verified in the firmware: radiator fan stage 0..3 (cooling fan actuation, the *_CFA constants: coolant thresholds C_TCO_*_CFA, speed limits C_VS_*_CFA, delay timers C_T_RTD_*_CFA). Stage 1 drives one pair of output bits (BFD78.10/.2), stage 2 another (BFD78.8/.0), stage 3 both. Only 0 and 1 were seen in your logs.&quot;&#013;&#010; ram address 0xC276&#013;&#010;Confidence: high.</desc>
    <parentcmdidhash>0xDAA83ACD</parentcmdidhash>
    <units>Radiator fan stage</units>
    <packetoffset>0x5C</packetoffset>
    <range low="0.000000" high="3.000000" />
    <alarms low="0.000000" high="255.000000" />
    <digcount>1</digcount>
    <outputtype>1</outputtype>
    <datatype>1</datatype>
    <MATH equation="X">
      <VAR varID="X" type="native" />
    </MATH>
  </ADXVALUE>

  <ADXVALUE id="TORQUEREQUEST" idhash="0x888569F3" title="tcs torque intervention.">
    <desc> tcs torque intervention: 164 = none, drops to 23 on hard launches with wheel spin then slowly increases, also triggered in logs where (iirc) i lost traction while moving. stayed 164 for launches with tcs off.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;according to claude the ram address is 0xC596</desc>
    <flags>0x00000004</flags>
    <parentcmdidhash>0xDAA83ACD</parentcmdidhash>
    <units>tcs torque intervention. (%)</units>
    <packetoffset>0x5D</packetoffset>
    <range low="0.000000" high="100.000000" />
    <alarms low="0.000000" high="165.000000" />
    <digcount>2</digcount>
    <outputtype>3</outputtype>
    <datatype>3</datatype>
    <unittype>3</unittype>
    <MATH equation="X/1.64">
      <VAR varID="X" type="native" />
    </MATH>
  </ADXVALUE>

