    <desc>Was 0 in all logs and never changed.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;according to claude &quot;VIM (variable intake manifold) output flags: bit 0 for the single-stage config, bits 1 and 2 for the two-stage config. They come from the ID_VIM_* maps and C_VS_MIN_VIM.&quot;&#013;&#010;its zero because &quot;C_CONF_VIM = 0, so VIM is disabled in this tune&quot;&#013;&#010;ram address 0xC249&#013;&#010;its confidence level is &quot;High&quot;</desc>
