  <ADXVALUE id="VBATCOMP" idhash="0x328649EE" title="Ignition coil dwell time (battery / rpm compensated)*">
    <desc>varies with battery voltage, thought could be some kind of voltage based compensation/adjustment, &#013;&#010;compared to some maps and it somewhat matched the shape of the axis of IP_TI_ADD_DLY__VB and IP_CPPWM_CPS_VB_ADD__VB&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;according to claude &quot;Verified in the firmware: Computed from IP_TD__VB__N (dwell time vs battery voltage and rpm, XDF equation 0.004*X ms) plus a signed correction (0x72240-0x72276 and 0x5F48C-0x5F4AC), and consumed by the ignition timing code at 0x7E97E (divided against the rpm period). TD = coil dwell, not an injector dead time (the injector dead-time table IP_TI_ADD_DLY__VB has no rpm axis). The shape match you saw with the VB axes is because both depend on battery voltage.&#013;&#010;Equation 0.004*X ms follows the table&apos;s unit.&quot;&#013;&#010;ram address 0xFA6A-0xFA6B&#013;&#010;Confidence: high for the identity, medium-high for the scale.</desc>
    <flags>0x00000002</flags>
    <parentcmdidhash>0xDAA83ACD</parentcmdidhash>
    <units>Ignition coil dwell time (battery / rpm compensated) (ms)</units>
    <packetoffset>0x61</packetoffset>
    <sizeinbits>16</sizeinbits>
    <range low="0.000000" high="25.000000" />
    <alarms low="0.000000" high="255.000000" />
    <digcount>1</digcount>
    <outputtype>1</outputtype>
    <datatype>3</datatype>
    <unittype>3</unittype>
    <MATH equation="X * 0.004">
      <VAR varID="X" type="native" />
    </MATH>
  </ADXVALUE>

